/*
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * K&A Client Diaries — Entry (alternate article template)
 * Docs/client-diaries-build-spec.md §3 — built from
 * Prototypes/client-diaries-entry-v1.html (approved by Suraj,
 * 10 Aug 2026, spec v2.0, section-order revision applied).
 *
 * ALTERNATE TEMPLATE, not the default article.json: this theme's
 * default templates/article.json (built for The Journal) applies to
 * every article in every blog by default. Client Diaries entries
 * need a structurally different template (different hero register,
 * a "Her Review" stinger block, alternating Look Spreads, etc.), so
 * each Client Diaries article must have this template assigned
 * manually per-article in Shopify Admin: Online Store -> Blog posts
 * -> [the client's entry] -> Theme template (right sidebar) ->
 * "diary". Until that's set, a new article in the "client-diaries"
 * blog would render with the Journal's default article.json instead
 * -- an operational step to flag to whoever creates each entry.
 *
 * Sections: Nav -> Entry Hero -> Her Review (B1, moved up per 10 Aug
 * 2026 direction) -> From the Atelier (B2) -> Look Spreads (C,
 * repeats per Look) -> More Diaries/Share (E) -> Appointment CTA
 * (reused ka-appointment) -> Footer. ka-nav is included explicitly
 * here (not a layout.theme.liquid global) exactly like templates/
 * article.json does for The Journal -- its fixed nav sits behind the
 * Entry Hero's own fixed return-link/scroll-progress row, identical
 * layering to the Journal article template.
 *
 * See sections/ka-diary-featured.liquid header comment for the full
 * data-model writeup (blog articles + metafields + metaobjects) and
 * the specific metafield/metaobject definitions that must be created
 * manually in Shopify Admin before any entry can be populated.
 *
 * Re-committed 2026-08-10 (deployment-verification re-push): this
 * file did not sync to the staging theme on the first push despite
 * committing/pushing cleanly to git -- same silent GitHub->Shopify
 * sync-failure pattern documented in CLAUDE.md's Deployment
 * Verification section (real incident, 2026-07-11). Confirmed via
 * Admin GraphQL theme.files spot-check after this re-push.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 */
